From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 03:21:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: cover native point clipping against the view
 volume

Metal keeps a point whose centre leaves the view volume as long as the
point's size still reaches the viewport. The conformance reference
rasterizer discards a point only when its depth leaves the volume, and
OpenGL requires the same rule, so applying the side planes to a point
centre makes Zink's wide points vanish at a viewport edge. Lock the
reported VK_POINT_CLIPPING_BEHAVIOR_USER_CLIP_PLANES_ONLY and the
rasterized result with a test that draws the eight large points of
dEQP-VK.clipping.clip_volume.clipped.large_points through the hardware
vertex stage and through a point-emitting geometry stage.
